    "question_type": "conceptual",
    "question_text": "List five main groups of natural plant growth regulators. Write a note on discovery, physiological functions and agricultural/horticultural applications of any one of them.",
    "question_latex": null,
    "mcq_options": [],
    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "Plant growth regulators are the chemical molecules secreted by plants affecting the physiological attributes of a plant. There are five main plant growth regulators: (i) Auxins, (ii) Gibberellic acid, (iii) Cytokinins, (iv) Ethylene, (v) Abscisic acid. Auxins were first observed by Charles Darwin and Francis Darwin, who noted the bending of coleoptiles towards light. They control plant cell growth, cause apical dominance, and have various horticultural applications.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Thus, auxins play a crucial role in plant growth and development.",
    "answer_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
